==Low German==

===Alternative forms===
* [[Morren]] (usually found as "Morr'n", might hence be just a misspelling of Morrn)
* [[Morrn]]

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|osx|nds}} {{term|morgan|lang=osx}} from {{proto|Germanic|murganaz|lang=nds}}. Cognate Dutch {{term|morgen|lang=nl}}, Old High German {{term|morgan|lang=goh}} (German {{term|Morgen|lang=de}}), Old East Norse {{term|morghon|lang=non}} (Danish {{term|morgen|lang=da}}, Swedish {{term|morgon|lang=sv}}), Old Norse {{term|morginn}}, {{term|morgunn}}; compare also (from a variant Germanic base) Old West Norse {{term|myrginn}}, Gothic {{term|𐌼𐌰𐌿𐍂𐌲𐌹𐌽𐍃|sc=Goth|tr=maurgins}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈmɔ͡ɐŋ̩/|lang=nds}}

===Noun===
